    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0381" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v22/pg353"/>

                <head>209. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Indonesia<anchor n="1" xml:id="d209-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-02-23T16:32:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                                1957—4:32 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1367. Advise soonest whether Embassy has since your 1961<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d209-f2"/> informed Indos of U.S. aid offer increase from fifteen to
                    twenty-five million. Otherwise believe offer should be withheld at least pending
                    further clarification political developments and Embassy’s recommendations U.S.
                    attitude aid policy.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d209-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d209-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d209-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 756D.5–MSP/2–657. Confidential. Drafted and approved in FE and cleared with SPA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d209-f2" n="2" xml:id="d209-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 1961 from Djakarta, February 6, stated that the Embassy had not informed
                    the Indonesian Government of U.S. approval of a $10 million line of credit for
                    Indonesia, in addition to the $15 million previously approved for fiscal year
                    1957. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d209-f3" n="3" xml:id="d209-f3-content">
                <p>The Embassy replied in telegram 2120 from Djakarta, February 25: “Have not
                    informed Indonesia US aid offer increase from 15 to 25 million. Thoroughly agree
                    with Department that offer of increase be withheld pending clarification
                    political development.” (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi> 756D.5–MSP/2–2557)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
